  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Pleasant Valley Colony was founded in 1989 as a daughter colony of New Rockport, joining the Lehrerleut Hutterites and embracing communal farming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pleasant_valley_colony_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pleasant Valley Colony sits 11 miles southwest of Belt and 19 miles southeast of Great Falls in eastern Cascade County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pleasant_Valley_Colony%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The colony shares labor and resources, raising about 400 dairy cows, 3,000 hogs, and irrigating gardens seasonally.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pleasant_valley_colony_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nestled on 4,200‑foot bench land north of the Little Belt Mountains, Pleasant Valley hosts barns, a slaughterhouse, kitchen, school, and barracks‑style homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pleasant_valley_colony_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The colony’s water comes from a deep well in the Madison limestone aquifer, safeguarded by a wellhead protection plan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pleasant_valley_colony_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 2017, a new Hill Top Hutterite Colony opened just four miles northwest of Pleasant Valley.",
